# Entry Main. A named actual that names no input of the data admits no form: the structural call is refused with 5
# before the value of the actual is read (step 21.7 K2). `Step\add(data := bump())`: the inputs of `Step` are `x`
# alone, there is no input `data`, and a call cannot supply a replacement parent. `bump` counts its calls: BEFORE is
# written, calls stays 0, AFTER is not.
# Norm: the book #structural-call (the names of the members of the actuals denote inputs of the data; a call cannot
# supply a replacement parent); #declaration-selection (an actual that binds no formal fails the pair).
int: before 0
int: calls 0
int: after 0
fn: bump () int
    node\calls := node\calls + 1
    return: 7
Box:
    int: q 1
end: Box
Step:
    int: x 5
    add:
        Box\q := x
    end: add
end: Step
Main:
    node\before := 1
    Step\add(data := bump())
    node\after := 2
